Z||000000||maryjane||06-30-2001||07:01 PM||||The emergency brake just failed inspection.Didn't hold at all. Their is plenty of pad left and the caliphers were replaced less than a year ago. The rear brakes work fine but their doesn't seem to be enough thread to take up the slack in the cable. The cable moves when I pull the brake handle, but not enough to hold. The cable isn't broken or disconnected anywhere. Any suggestions? Cables stretched maybe?<BR>84 Se||||reg||1
Z||000001||Vader||06-30-2001||08:45 PM||||It isn't uncommon to have the front e-brake cable come apart in the housing.  The plastic coating delaminates from the steel cable and starts to get the cable bound so it won't release fully.  Then the ratcheting levers won't adjust correctly to provide good braking.  A replacement cable can be had for just about $21.00 (Wagner F111055, Bendix C1423, or Pioneer/Barnes CA-5593).  It takes a couple of hours to change the cable if you are meticulous abot getting the trim and inner fenders back into correct alignment.<P>The rear (left and right) cables aren't terribly expensive either, and might be worth replacing if there is any sign of binding.  Since those cables are twisted and bent less than the front piece, they might be O.K.  Two out of three of my Fieros had bad front cables.<P>------------------<BR>"<I>Let the bodies hit the floor!</I>"||||reg||2
Z||000002||maryjane||06-30-2001||09:11 PM||||thanks, Jane has it at work right now, I'll check it out tomorrow, front to back. We never use the hand brake except during inspection, that is probably one of the problems.<BR>Don||||reg||1
Z||000003||Vader||06-30-2001||09:27 PM||||Yup, it's one of those things.  Either use it always, or never use it.  If you have safety inspections, you should probably get in the habit of using it frequently, or the actuator levers and screws at the rear calipers will be the next item on the failure list.<P>Frankly, I don't think they could have possibly designed a weaker E-brake system.  It must have been some of those recently-hired Chrysler engineers that GM felt sorry for in the mid-80s.  The same calipers on F-cars caused a recall due to poor E-brake performance.  Why would it be any better on the P-car?  I've been able to keep mine free by making a habit of applying clean brake fluid to the actuator screws when doing a chassis lube.  Laugh if you want, but that is the factory recommended procedure on these POS calipers.<P>------------------<BR>"<I>Let the bodies hit the floor!</I>"||||reg||2
Z||000004||fierobaby||06-30-2001||10:59 PM||||anyone knoe if its illegal not to have an e-brake? I don't have one....the cable was cut... am I going to have to reconnect it or am I ok without it? plus for shows do they check that when they judge?<P>------------------<BR>1984 Sweet Candy Apple red Fiero sport coupe :-D<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Fierowrecker||06-30-2001||11:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierobaby:<BR><B>anyone knoe if its illegal not to have an e-brake? I don't have one....the cable was cut... am I going to have to reconnect it or am I ok without it? plus for shows do they check that when they judge?<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hate to say it, but it is a federal standard to have e-brakes...<BR>If you get a state inspection, it is one of the things they check...<BR>In Michigan, we don't have state inspections, but a cop can ask you to be inpected on the side of the road...<BR>Most of the time they issue repair and report tickets for the non-functional equipment...<BR>crash...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||btoth||07-01-2001||11:20 AM||||They don't check 'em here in Ohio.  Mine was broken since the day I got it.  I had them fixed and they still only work on one side because no one seems to be able to adjust them correctly.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  I don't know anyone except Fiero owners that use their parking brake (e-brake, whatever) with an auto trans.  What a dumb design.||||reg||1
